            <h3>Provida SFA: offline-first sales platform</h3>
            <span class="lvl-tag">WORLD 2025 · MAIN QUEST</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          Sales reps in the field order without signal. Orders queue on-device with idempotency
          keys and sync safely when the network returns, with no duplicates and no lost work. The app
          tracks customer visits and stock counts, and closes the day with reports: sales
          history with order-status breakdowns, end-of-day summaries, and activity maps.
        </p>
        <p class="chips">
          <span class="chip sm">Next.js (PWA)</span><span class="chip sm">TypeScript</span>
          <span class="chip sm">Tailwind CSS</span><span class="chip sm">IndexedDB sync queue</span>
        </p>
        <div class="term">
          <div class="term-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>level01.log</span></div>
          <pre class="code">// Concept — a stable idempotency key rides with every queued order,
// so a retry after a flaky network can never create a duplicate.
queue.enqueue('order.create', order.withIdempotencyKey());</pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="level">
        <div class="level-head">
          <span class="lvl-no">02</span>
